WEBVTT

00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:13.370
MCP lets your AI tools work with your notes through the running app. Off by default; this PC only.

00:00:13.370 --> 00:00:26.470
Settings > MCP: switch it on, write your rules, create one token per client - shown once, stored as a hash.

00:00:26.470 --> 00:00:39.910
Connected: Claude Desktop reads the rules first, then works - every call lands in the audit log.

00:00:39.910 --> 00:00:54.630
The new page sits right below the source, exactly as the rules say. The bell reports every write.

00:00:54.630 --> 00:01:00.967
Scoped tokens are the hard limit: read, write or full. Rules are what you ask; the audit log is what happened.

